{"id": "v20-exceptions-rust-panicked",
 "asserts": "`chain.terminal: \"panicked\"` earns the PANICKED disposition, and the verdict quotes the frame the trace says unwound while holding the chain -- never that the panic happened BECAUSE of the `Err` (design R8). The holder is DERIVED, not carried: the chain's last event fired in `inner`, which returned `err`, and the innermost unwound frame walking outward is `run`, so the verdict names `f1` and not `f2`. The unwind is the frame's own `closed_by`/`unwind_exc` evidence -- the same evidence `tree` renders as `!! panic(..)` -- and no panic RAISE event exists here at all, so `panics:` is silent while the disposition still stands. This is the value's first conformance vector; it was pinned only by `tests/test_exceptions_rust.py` before 2026-09-08.",
